            {
                "entry_id": "0a25b399-a571-3932-8b77-28a42a1cddbc",
                "word": "ent",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ac4db418-8025-4965-be24-e4967ecd38c2",
                        "entry_id": "0a25b399-a571-3932-8b77-28a42a1cddbc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "ents"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "24b6cf9d-805b-3bc4-b84b-6978d26591f0",
                        "entry_id": "0a25b399-a571-3932-8b77-28a42a1cddbc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A large, fictional, humanoid, walking tree in works by J. R. R. Tolkien."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "062cf138-5593-4a1a-8b68-13a1cb46a6b2",
                                "sense_id": "24b6cf9d-805b-3bc4-b84b-6978d26591f0",
                                "text": "[…]and that fine young ent Quickbeam is merely a minor crux in an Old English glossary (the name Quickbeam means 'living tree' in Old English)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "15c6164c-9d76-4704-a179-d8fde284d178",
                                "sense_id": "24b6cf9d-805b-3bc4-b84b-6978d26591f0",
                                "text": "But this should not lead to complete avoidance, as if it is like some dire incursion of triffids or ents."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6b4f4fc-32ab-4ef7-8d31-cdfe7ecc0f25",
                                "sense_id": "24b6cf9d-805b-3bc4-b84b-6978d26591f0",
                                "text": "Somewhere, ents and manitous laugh grimly For, despite all this, the trees lasted much longer Than most of the presents, and all of the holiday spirit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c012daee-48bc-4b0a-b1fe-3b29eeb7f011",
                                "sense_id": "24b6cf9d-805b-3bc4-b84b-6978d26591f0",
                                "text": "Hello, my good friend, myself I present. Not human, nor tree, for I am an ent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "932701d2-4ffc-4387-9813-62dacba11738",
                                "sense_id": "24b6cf9d-805b-3bc4-b84b-6978d26591f0",
                                "text": "In The Lords of the Rings there are dark forces in the forest—the Huorn. Huorn are ents who have become more treeish, gone rogue. They can still move and speak, but only with the ents."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8f0f8ac2-0428-4aea-a06d-fd5bcbdffd3a",
                        "source_entry_id": "0a25b399-a571-3932-8b77-28a42a1cddbc",
                        "source_sense_id": "24b6cf9d-805b-3bc4-b84b-6978d26591f0",
                        "source_sense_description": "a fictional large talking tree",
                        "target_lang_word": "ent",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1f903b81-803a-405a-9933-786028693100",
                        "source_entry_id": "0a25b399-a571-3932-8b77-28a42a1cddbc",
