            {
                "entry_id": "32153f42-2783-3b8a-932d-841bea854d56",
                "word": "Ent",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "dc34956e-2dc8-4e60-a2cc-7bb21a468de1",
                        "entry_id": "32153f42-2783-3b8a-932d-841bea854d56",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Ents"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cc9ae04b-580d-30bf-91a5-3d07571b7b46",
                        "entry_id": "32153f42-2783-3b8a-932d-841bea854d56",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative letter-case form of ent."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7f5e4f5-6d3d-46e3-8718-d0a15fa8f366",
                                "sense_id": "cc9ae04b-580d-30bf-91a5-3d07571b7b46",
                                "text": "The strange words and names that the Hobbits record as used by Treebeard and other Ents are thus Elvish, or fragments of Elf-speech strung together in Ent-fashion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "21a7d634-40f7-46f7-a3e4-a2f79e1df06f",
                                "sense_id": "cc9ae04b-580d-30bf-91a5-3d07571b7b46",
                                "text": "Ents and Entwives, Jack thought crazily. BAD Ents and Entwives."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e8953a6-1289-4599-9203-1347935290c2",
                                "sense_id": "cc9ae04b-580d-30bf-91a5-3d07571b7b46",
                                "text": "Tolkien's Treebeard, his Ent creation, was inspired by Lewis, especially his sometimes emphatic deep voice"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e5470b3-375b-4d80-a9ee-3ae66bef2b42",
                                "sense_id": "cc9ae04b-580d-30bf-91a5-3d07571b7b46",
                                "text": "Tolkien perhaps speaks for himself when he has Treebeard confess that \"nobody cares for the woods as I care for them,\" and when this same Ent also warns that \"the withering of all woods may be drawing near\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "80ccc42a-0ece-43a9-82f6-ca66e35159a8",
                                "sense_id": "cc9ae04b-580d-30bf-91a5-3d07571b7b46",
                                "text": "The Ents are a race of giant, tree-like people. Their purpose is to protect the electrons, though some align themselves with holes. However, as the great arrays have grown, the number of Ents has dwindled. Now they are said only to be found in the darkest and most mysterious of laboratories."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
